                "Grain_Size_Units": "",
                "Microstructural_Features": "the surface of the coating is tight but uneven and undulating. has a complex structure consisting of a hard phase mixed with a softer matrix that acts as a binder, facilitating the adhesion of the ceramic to the substrate and the cohesion between the particles, this forming a compact and stable coating on the substrate. the coatings have a smooth surface with fine grains. the powder is dented at the substrate surface and much thinner than the original powder. cracking and breaking of the Cr3C2 particles observed. No cracks on the coating, homogeneous microstructure. "
            },
            "Notes": "0.05 M TAA concentration"
